{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Ho, land.</b> 'Ho' is an expression of calling, like 'Ho, ho, flee from the land of the north' (Zechariah 2:10)." "<b>Buzzing of wings.</b> Doubled from 'shadow,' for it is a broad land." "<b>Beyond the rivers of Cush.</b> The name of the kingdom of Assyria."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:08.822805942Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}